{"abstract":[{"text":"Connect and run commands on the different applications on a YubiKey. The framework support connecting using NFC, Lightning and USB.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"YubiKit","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"beta":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"13.0"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"YubiKit"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"documentation-header.png"}],"color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"green"},"externalID":"YubiKit"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The YubiKit Swift SDK provides a modern async\/await version of the YubiKit framework, making it easy to integrate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Swift and SwiftUI based applications. The async\/await syntax provides an easy to read and powerful way of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"creating connections and sending commands to the different applications on the YubiKey.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This SDK does not perform zeroization of sensitive data in memory. Cryptographic keys, PIN tokens,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and other secrets are not securely erased when no longer in use. This is currently out of scope but may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"addressed in a future release.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Warning","type":"aside","style":"warning"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Prepar